     Upon successful completion, the value 0 is returned; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The ggeettrrlliimmiitt() and sseettrrlliimmiitt() system calls will fail if:

     [EFAULT]           The address specified for _r_l_p is invalid.

     [EPERM]            The limit specified to sseettrrlliimmiitt() would have raised
                        the maximum limit value, and the caller is not the su‐
                        per-user.

